    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **276 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner creation limit by adding a step to the OfficeFloor `POST /api/owners` pipeline, following the project's existing patterns (matching how the duplicate-telephone and duplicate-email rejections work).\n\n**New files:**\n- `RejectDailyOwnerLimit.java` \u2014 function that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today; throws when 20 already exist.\n- `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java` \u2014 checked exception (so it surfaces on the `throws` clause for OfficeFloor escalation matching).\n- `DailyOwnerLimitExceededExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 escalation handler responding **400 Bad Request** with a `ProblemDetail` body, matching the other handlers.\n- `...DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `rejectDailyLimit` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) after the duplicate-email check and before `assignMembershipNumber`. It runs after `build`, so the registration date is already assigned.\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java` \u2014 added `createOwnerRejectedWhenDailyLimitReached`, which seeds 20 owners registered today and asserts the 21st POST returns 400.\n\nNotes on correctness:\n- The limit is 20 owners per day, keyed on registration date (`LocalDate.now()`), exactly as specified.\n- Seed data owners have `NULL` registration dates, so they don't count toward today's total, and the existing `createOwnerSuccess`/duplicate tests (which create only 1\u20132 owners today) remain unaffected.",
